<p class="mb-3">
  Your enterprise has made GitHub <%= Copilot::COPILOT_CODE_REVIEW %> available to all members of the organization. To let members without Copilot seats in <%= link_to @organization_login, user_url(@organization_login) %> use it, enable the organization policy.
</p>

<p class="mb-3">
  This policy allows members without Copilot seats to get AI-powered review suggestions directly in pull requests, and your organization will be charged for their usage.
</p>

<p class="mb-3">
  <b>How to enable</b>
</p>

<ol class="mb-3">
  <li>Go to <b><%= link_to "Organization settings → Copilot → Policies", settings_org_copilot_policies_url(@organization) %></b></li>
  <li>Enable <b>Allow members without a Copilot license to use Copilot code review in <%= GitHub.host_name %></b></li>
</ol>

<div class="mb-3" style="text-align: center;">
  <img src="<%= mailer_static_asset_path("images/email/copilot/copilot-code-review-direct-billing-policy-toggle.png") %>" alt="Org settings screen with 'Allow members without a Copilot license to use Copilot code review in <%= GitHub.host_name %>' toggle highlighted" width="514">
</div>

<%= render(Mail::ButtonComponent.new(
  text: "Get started with #{Copilot::COPILOT_CODE_REVIEW} now",
  url: Copilot::CODE_REVIEW_REQUEST_DOCS_URL,
  classes: "btn-primary btn-large"
)) %>

<% content_for :footer_text do %>
  <p>
    You are receiving this because you are an administrator of the <%= link_to "@#{@organization_login}", user_url(@organization_login) %> organization.
  </p>
<% end %>
